                <pb facs="0577" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg465"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Fox.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June 2,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The following telegram has been received from the legation at Lima (supra, June
                    1):</p>
                <p>Hasten solemnly to impress the Government of Ecuador with the fact that by
                    failure to take similar action and to make their acceptance unencumbered with
                    premature arguments they would assume before the world the responsibility of
                    jeopardizing the mediation and of the grave consequences which might follow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
